{
    "name": "Aqueducts",
    "category": "tfc:agriculture",
    "icon": "tfc:rock/aqueduct/shale",
    "pages": [
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "text": "$(thing)Aqueducts$() are a tool used for moving $(thing)Fluids$() around. Since $(item)Wooden Buckets$(), are not able to transport water sources, $(thing)Aqueducts$() exist to move fluids horizontally any distance to their destination. They can be used to transport any type of water―including $(thing)Fresh Water$(), $(thing)Salt Water$(), and $(thing)Hot Spring Water$()―as well as $(thing)Lava$().$(br)Aqueducts with plain water in them can $(l:agriculture/growing_crops#hydration)hydrate farmland$()."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "text": "In order to use an $(thing)Aqueduct$(), you must simply connect them in a horizontal pattern, and place one end adjacent to either a $(thing)Source$() or $(thing)Falling$() water. After waiting a short while, water will begin to flow through the aqueduct network, and out the other end.$(br2)$(bold)Note:$() If aqueducts are removed, water will cease flowing, and $(thing)Aqueducts$() will not create permanent source blocks―any water will disappear after the aqueducts are removed."
        },
